{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788201895,"nonce":"tf7YUqrQzlxGmMTyhrVOrnec5zU=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCORRECTED — three body-level errors. Two of them mean the acceptance FAILS on the\nbench as written, and one means the issue asks for work that is already shipped.\nThe DESIGN-level argument (this is a policy, not a judgement call) survives all\nthree intact; it is the mechanics underneath that are off.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — \"NOTHING CURRENTLY SURFACES DOWNED ENEMIES\" IS FALSE. MOST OF\nTHE READ THIS ISSUE ASKS FOR IS ALREADY SHIPPED.\n=====================================================================\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/PawnSerializer.Brief` already emits, per pawn,\n`[\"id\"] = pawn.thingIDNumber`, `[\"at\"] = Positions.Out(pawn.Position)`, and\n\n    if (pawn.Downed) flags.Add(\"downed\");\n    ...\n    if (health.hediffSet.BleedRateTotal \u003e 0.01f) flags.Add(\"bleeding\");\n\nand `Source/AutoRimmer/PawnVerbs.Pawns` skips only `p.Dead` and\n`PawnSafe.Hidden(p, map)` — it does NOT skip `p.Downed`. `PawnSafe.FilterClasses`\nmaps `\"hostile\"` to `ClassHostile`. So `pawns {filter:\"hostile\"}` returns id,\nposition, `downed` and `bleeding` for every visible downed raider TODAY.\n\nThe acceptance bullet \"a read that surfaces downed hostiles: id, position,\nwhether stabilised\" is therefore about 90% already met, and the one missing\nfield — \"stabilised\" — has no vanilla referent at all (Correction 3). Re-scope\nthis bullet before dispatch or a worker builds a second read that duplicates\n`pawns`.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — STEP 2 AND STEP 3 CONTRADICT EACH OTHER, AND THE ACCEPTANCE\nBULLET BUILT ON STEP 3 WILL FAIL\n=====================================================================\n\nStep 3's claim is \"a raider woke up needs no decision at all because seek-at-will\nre-engages on its own\", and the acceptance turns that into \"a raider that wakes\nmid-procedure is engaged by seek pawns with NO new agent decision\".\n\n`seekandkill/Source/SeekAndKill/SeekRegistry.ShouldSeek`, verbatim:\n\n    return pawn.Spawned\n        \u0026\u0026 !pawn.Drafted\n        \u0026\u0026 !pawn.InMentalState\n        \u0026\u0026 pawn.Faction == Faction.OfPlayer\n        \u0026\u0026 !pawn.RaceProps.Animal\n        \u0026\u0026 !PSInterop.IsPsAvatar(pawn)\n        \u0026\u0026 IsToggled(pawn);\n\n`!pawn.Drafted`. And step 2 — finish off downed enemies — requires a DRAFTED pawn:\n`RimWorld/FloatMenuOptionProvider_DraftedAttack` is\n`protected override bool Drafted =\u003e true; protected override bool Undrafted =\u003e false;`.\n\nSo every pawn executing step 2 has seek-at-will suppressed for as long as it\nstays drafted. Step 3 holds only for the pawns you did not draft. On a\nthree-colonist M1 colony with two drafted for finish-off, \"no new agent decision\"\nis simply not true. The procedure needs an explicit undraft step — which is also\nwhat 4.2's amendment and 4.3's amendment independently ask for, from the other\ndirection. Three issues are circling the same missing step; this is the one where\nit changes a stated mechanism rather than a habit.\n\n(Separately, the CITATION for \"a downed pawn is not a threat\" is wrong by member.\n`ShouldSeek` is a DOER-eligibility gate and names no target. The target-side\nexclusions are elsewhere in SeekAndKill — `JobGiver_SquadSeek` has\n`\u0026\u0026 (hostile is not Pawn enemy || !enemy.Downed)`, and `ThreatCluster`,\n`SelfDefenseUtility` and `SquadManager` all exclude downed targets. The\nconclusion is right; the member cited does not support it.)\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 3 — \"STABILISED\" HAS NO VANILLA REFERENT\n=====================================================================\n\nThere is no `Stabilize` JobDef or RecipeDef anywhere in the vanilla+DLC def tree\n(the only `Stabiliz*` hits are `MechStabilizer` buildings, unrelated). The\nacceptance word is borrowed from a mod concept. The readable proxies are\n`hediffSet.BleedRateTotal` and per-hediff `Tended`, both of which\n`PawnSerializer` already surfaces (`bleeding` flag, `bleed_rate`). Restate the\nacceptance against one of those, or it cannot be satisfied.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED — AND THE CENTRAL ARGUMENT IS INTACT\n=====================================================================\n\n- `DigestVerb.ThreatSection` verbatim:\n  `if (p.Downed || p.Dead || !p.HostileTo(Faction.OfPlayer)) continue;`\n  So `threats.hostiles == 0` really is \"no hostile is STANDING\". CONFIRMED.\n- `p.Downed` is a safe read: `Verse/Pawn.Downed =\u003e health.Downed` and\n  `Pawn_HealthTracker.Downed =\u003e healthState == PawnHealthState.Down`. A field\n  compare, no lazy init, no Rand. CONFIRMED.\n- \"Do not conflate `DangerRating` with `hostiles`; they disagree\" — CONFIRMED,\n  and the mechanism is fully readable. `RimWorld/DangerWatcher.CalculateDangerRating`\n  is a threshold function over SUMMED combat power\n  (`num \u003c 150f \u0026\u0026 num \u003c= colonists*18f` -\u003e Low; `num \u003e 400f` -\u003e High), refreshed\n  at most once per 101 ticks by its getter\n  (`if (Find.TickManager.TicksGame \u003e lastUpdateTick + 101)`), and it drops pawns\n  that `GenHostility.AffectsStoryDanger` excludes — `LordJob_DefendPoint` /\n  `LordJob_MechanoidDefendBase` groups not on attack duty, dormant\n  `CompCanBeDormant` pawns — as well as everything `IsPotentialThreat` drops\n  (`PanicFlee`, prisoners, `!pawn.Awake()`, deactivated mechs). A live\n  \"three raiders, DangerRating None\" reading is fully explicable by any of those.\n  Which one it actually was NEEDS THE BENCH.\n  Note the file is `RimWorld/DangerWatcher.cs`, not `Verse/` — `DigestVerb`'s own\n  comment gets this right and the issue body does not.\n- Allow Tool is not on the bench. CONFIRMED: `_RimWorld-Agent/Mods/` holds 33\n  mods, none of them AllowTool, and the generated `ModsConfig.xml` has no\n  `unlimitedhugs.allowtool`. Worth stating for the next reader: it IS present in\n  the user's MAIN profile config, so anyone \"verifying\" this against\n  `~/.config/unity3d/...` will get the wrong answer.\n- 4.1 does specify `checklists/morning.md` and a `trigger-context` frontmatter\n  field. CONFIRMED against `96d9315`.\n\n=====================================================================\nFOUR THINGS THE ISSUE MISSES\n=====================================================================\n\n1. **THE TRIGGER HAS NO FOG FILTER, AND THAT IS A DEFECT IN THE PREDICATE.**\n   `ThreatSection`'s hostile loop never calls `PawnSafe.Hidden`, while the FIRES\n   block eight lines below it does (`try { if (f.Position.Fogged(map)) continue; }\n   catch { continue; }`). So one standing hostile in unexplored fog pins\n   `threats.hostiles` above zero indefinitely and the procedure never fires. And\n   because `PawnVerbs.Pawns` DOES fog-filter, `pawns {filter:\"hostile\"}` and\n   `threats.hostiles` can legitimately disagree — the agent sees zero hostiles\n   and the trigger says three. This is the same class of bug as the\n   `DangerRating`-vs-`hostiles` conflation the issue was filed to correct, one\n   layer in. Fix it, or state the trigger as\n   `pawns {filter:\"hostile\"}.total == 0` instead.\n\n2. **THE ORDERS ARE ALREADY SHIPPED.** `rescue`, `capture`, `arrest`, `carry` and\n   `attack` are all live verbs in `Source/AutoRimmer/PawnOrderVerbs.cs`, and\n   `TakeToBedGate` already reproduces each provider's gate clause by clause\n   (including `ProviderGate(..., mechanoidCanDo: false, requiresManipulation: true)`,\n   the `FloatMenuOptionProvider` base preconditions). The issue reads as though\n   the procedure must build them. It must only SEQUENCE them. That materially\n   shrinks the work and should be said, because it changes whether this is a\n   wave-3 or a wave-4 item.\n\n3. **THE FINISH-OFF PATH BURNS THE SHARED RAND STREAM AND WRITES SCRIBED STATE.**\n   `FloatMenuUtility.GetMeleeAttackAction` gates on\n   `pawn.meleeVerbs.TryGetMeleeVerb(target.Thing) == null`, which falls through to\n   `Pawn_MeleeVerbs.ChooseMeleeVerb` — `bool flag = Rand.Chance(0.04f);` then\n   `TryRandomElementByWeight(...)`, with NO `Rand.PushState`, and it writes\n   `curMeleeVerb`, which `Pawn_MeleeVerbs.ExposeData` scribes. The existing\n   `attack` verb already pays this, so it is not new — but a procedure that fires\n   finish-off across N raiders x M colonists multiplies it, and a deterministic\n   procedure that perturbs the RNG once per victim deserves a line in its own\n   spec.\n\n4. **THE MODAL HAZARD IS ON ARREST ONLY, AND IS ALREADY DODGED.**\n   `FloatMenuOptionProvider_Arrest`'s action delegate ends in\n   `TutorUtility.DoModalDialogIfNotKnown(ConceptDefOf.ArrestingCreatesEnemies, ...)`;\n   `PawnOrderVerbs.cs` documents it and does not invoke the delegate. Rescue,\n   Capture and the drafted-attack path are clean — their delegates only call\n   `PlayerKnowledgeDatabase.KnowledgeDemonstrated`. Recording it so the procedure\n   does not re-litigate the question.\n\nSmall: `DangerWatcher.DangerRating`'s getter is itself a write-on-read\n(`dangerRatingInt`, `lastUpdateTick`). Neither is scribed — `DangerWatcher` has no\n`ExposeData` — so it is benign for the save, but it consumes the 101-tick budget\nfor whoever reads next.\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE — ITEM BY ITEM\n=====================================================================\n\n- \"a read that surfaces downed hostiles: id, position, whether stabilised\" —\n  mostly already true (Correction 1); \"stabilised\" untestable (Correction 3).\n- \"runs on `threats.hostiles` reaching 0\" — testable, but the predicate is wrong\n  on a partly-unexplored map (Miss 1).\n- \"re-entrant — if the count flips back up mid-procedure it yields, and resumes\n  after\" — testable in principle; `dev:damage` / `HealthUtility.DamageUntilDowned`\n  are already used in `DevVerbs`/`JournalVerbs` so the fixture is reachable. But\n  the issue never says WHERE the resume cursor lives (a tick? a journal seq? a\n  GameComponent field?), and \"resumes after\" is not checkable without that.\n  Underspecified.\n- \"Rescue precedes finish-off, and the reason is stated where a reader will see\n  it\" — a code-comment review, not a mechanical check. Fine, label it as one.\n- \"Finish-off is a flag, defaulting on only while no prison exists\" — the flag is\n  testable; \"no prison exists\" NEEDS A NAMED READ. Nothing computes it today. The\n  two candidates are `RestUtility.FindBedFor(..., GuestStatus.Prisoner)` returning\n  null, or a `Building_Bed.ForPrisoners` scan. **Note also that `rooms` already\n  publishes `prison_cell` per room (`PlaceVerbs.Brief`: `[\"prison_cell\"] = room.IsPrisonCell`),\n  so a third and cheapest option exists — see the verification comment on\n  `e1c072e`, where the same fact is the largest correction.** Pick one on-issue.\n- \"a raider that wakes mid-procedure engaged by seek pawns with NO new agent\n  decision\" — WILL FAIL as written (Correction 2).\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- Which of `AffectsStoryDanger`'s exclusions produced the live\n  \"swordsman hauls wood while three raiders live\" reading. I enumerated the\n  candidates from source; I did not reproduce it. It is one bench run to settle\n  and it would be worth settling, because the DESIGN decisions-log entry cites\n  that incident as the worked example.\n- That the fog gap (Miss 1) has actually bitten. The asymmetry is read from the\n  code; I have no observation of it.","files":null}]}